.TH "rtcCommitBuffer" "3" "" "" "Embree Ray Tracing Kernels 4"
.SS NAME
.IP
.EX
rtcCommitBuffer \- commits buffer content from host to device
.EE
.SS SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include <embree4/rtcore.h>

void rtcCommitBuffer(RTCBuffer buffer);
.EE
.SS DESCRIPTION
If the buffer was created using \f[CR]rtcNewBufferHostDevice\f[R] the
\f[CR]rtcCommitBuffer\f[R] function commits changes of the host buffer
data to the device.
This call is not necessary if the buffer was created with a non SYCL
Embree device.
.PP
The call to \f[CR]rtcCommitBuffer\f[R] will internally use a temporary
SYCL queue and wait for the memory copy to finish.
The function \f[CR]rtcCommitBufferWithQueue\f[R] can be used to
asyncronously copy the data to the device.
.SS EXIT STATUS
On failure an error code is set that can be queried using
\f[CR]rtcGetDeviceError\f[R].
.SS SEE ALSO
[rtcCommitBufferWithQueue] [rtcNewBufferHostDevice]
